🧱 AdventureWorks Data Warehouse – Silver Layer (Sales Schema)
📌 Overview

This project implements the Silver Layer transformation of the AdventureWorks dataset, focusing on the Sales domain.

The goal of the Silver layer is to:

Clean and standardize Bronze/raw data
Combine normalized tables into analysis-friendly entities
Reduce join complexity for downstream users
Prepare structured datasets for Gold layer (BI / Power BI dashboards)

🏗️ Architecture

🔹 Bronze Layer (Source)
Raw tables from adventureworks2019
Highly normalized
Not optimized for analytics

🔹 Silver Layer (This Implementation)
Created in: adventureworks_silver
Schema used: sales, production
Uses SQL Views to:
Flatten relationships
Add business context
Handle nulls and defaults
Improve readability

🎯 Design Principles
1. Domain-Based Modeling

Instead of keeping tables fragmented, data is grouped into business entities:

Customer
Sales
Product
Payment
Salesperson

2. View-Based Transformation
No physical duplication of data
Views act as logical data models
Ensures:
Maintainability
Real-time reflection of source updates

3. Data Enrichment

Multiple tables are combined to provide:

Full names (concat_ws)
Geographic hierarchy (City → State → Country)
Product categorization
Sales reasons and metadata
4. Null Handling & Defaults
COALESCE() used for missing values
Default labels like 'Other' for unknown categories
5. Reusable CTEs

Common patterns extracted using CTEs:

PersonAddress
PersonDetails
product_detail
sales_reason
📊 Implemented Views
🧑‍💼 sales.Customer_Demographics

Purpose:
Unified customer profile including:

Personal details
Address & geography
Store association
Sales territory

Key Transformations:

Combines Customer, Person, Store, Territory
Resolves both individual customers and store customers
Maps SalesPerson via store relationship
💳 sales.Payment_details

Purpose:
Customer payment and credit card insights

Key Features:

Joins:
PersonCreditCard
CreditCard
Person + Address
Includes:
Card type
Expiry
Customer location
🏷️ sales.Product_Offers

Purpose:
Product pricing and promotional insights

Key Features:

Combines:
Product
Special Offers
Adds:
Discount %
Offer duration
Quantity conditions
🧾 sales.Sales_Details

Purpose:
Core fact-like dataset for sales analytics

Grain:
➡️ One row per Sales Order Line Item

Includes:

Product hierarchy
Sales reason classification
Pricing and totals
Order lifecycle dates

Enhancements:

Default handling for missing sales reasons
Combines Header + Detail tables
🧑‍💼 sales.SalesPerson_Details

Purpose:
Performance and organizational view of sales staff

Includes:

Sales quotas and performance metrics
Territory mapping
Tax rates by region
Store relationships
🧠 Key Modeling Decisions
✔️ Denormalization for Analytics

Instead of:

Many joins at query time

We provide:

Pre-joined, wide datasets
✔️ Business-Friendly Naming
Product_Category instead of IDs
SalesReason instead of codes
✔️ Separation of Concerns
Each view serves a clear analytical purpose
Avoids "one giant table" anti-pattern
🚀 Benefits
Faster query development
Easier Power BI integration
Reduced SQL complexity for analysts
Scalable for Gold Layer (KPIs, Aggregations)
🔮 Next Steps (Gold Layer)
Build fact/dimension model:
FactSales
DimCustomer
DimProduct
Add:
Aggregations
KPIs (Revenue, Profit, Growth)
Optimize for reporting tools
🏁 Conclusion

This Silver layer demonstrates how to:

Transform normalized OLTP schema into analytical datasets
Apply real-world data engineering practices
Prepare data for scalable BI solutions
